        "code": {
          "text": "Suicidal thoughts and safety assessment"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Passive suicidal ideation: “easier if I didn’t wake up.” Last week, thought of overdosing on partner’s sleeping tablets. No current active plan or intent today; reports ambivalence, “don’t really care what happens to me half the time.” Formal suicidality screen today assessed moderate risk. No previous suicide attempts; history of superficial cutting as a teenager. Patient is engaging and contracting to safety."
      }
